    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** commanding the top spot in our lineup projections with an elite 81.21 efficiency score. Facing Jacob Lopez, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** benefits from a favorable 4.67 xERA matchup and a projected #3 spot in the order that maximizes his run-production potential. Following him, **Jackson Merrill** (69.12) is our most efficient speed-inclusive play; his matchup against a mid-tier arm in Irvin yields a strong platoon advantage that elevates his floor significantly. While **Gunnar Henderson** (65.79) and **Coby Mayo** (65.57) are both tagged as strong starts, they face a tougher assignment against Cantillo. However, both benefit from significant park factors that effectively mitigate the impact of the opposing starter, keeping their offensive upside well within the reliable range.\n\n**Wade Meckler** (51.27) and **Drake Baldwin** (48.10) hover in the marginal territory, representing the \"efficiency floor\" for the squad today. **Wade Meckler** earned the nod over other depth options largely due to a favorable batting order placement (#3), which compounds the value of his platoon edge against Bello. **Kyle Tucker** (55.52) remains a start despite facing the highest-skill arm of the day in Chase Burns; his elite base projection keeps him in the lineup, though his output is subject to the highest volatility due to the SP's low xERA. We continue to monitor the status of **Luis Robert Jr.**, **Andy Pages**, and **Jordan Westburg**, all of whom remain on the IL, while **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** is inactive today due to a team off-day. \n\nThe optimizer\u2019s toughest decision centered on balancing the limited availability of our healthy bench against the rigid game-cap constraints. Ultimately, the projection models favored the consistency of **Wade Meckler** over potential high-upside gambles from speculative call-ups like **Jacob Wilson** or **Heliot Ramos**, as the latter group lacked the clear order-positioning benefits required to break the 50-point threshold. We remain cautious regarding **Drake Baldwin** and **Kyle Tucker**, as their respective lineups are currently pending; should either be dropped from their assumed spots in the order, their efficiency scores will be subject to an immediate downward revision.",
